/-- **SUF-CMA of SLH-DSA at any SHA-2 parameter set `S`** — internal algorithms (FIPS 205 Alg. 18–20); byte-string keys, messages, signatures; final form: twelve standard-model advantages, tight caps, memoising class adversaries `bTcrArM`.
Instance of `Reduction.slhdsa_sha2_128s_bytes_suf_cma_final` (`Reduction/HeadlineFinal.lean`).  Which hash function each term is about depends on `S`:
see the per-set theorems and `MReduction/Audit.lean`. -/
theorem slhdsa_sha2_bytes_suf_cma_final (S : Sha2Set)
    (optRand : PublicKeyCore S.prims.core → ProbComp S.prims.Y)
    (pkSeedDist : ProbComp S.prims.PkSeed)
    (F : BytesStrongForger S.vp S.prims (codec S) optRand pkSeedDist) :
    SignatureAlg.strongUnforgeableAdvantage ProbCompRuntime.probComp F ≤
      betaSufFinalMemo (bytesToTypedS F).toUnforgeableAdversary :=
  slhdsa_bytes_suf_cma_final (structural S) F

